# TUI-DESIGN-3 §1.8 edge 1: a key pasted with a trailing CR — the App splits the chunk into the text and the Enter it ended with,
# `sanitizeKeyInput` strips the whitespace and the Enter saves the clean key (four file keys from one paste); `Verify now?` follows
# (`n` skips — JEVCODE_ASSERT_NO_NETWORK stays untouched), then the idle console. The `[setup] spend caps` item is written while the
# wizard is still on `verify` (the save resolved the controller's prompt), so run-smoke.sh greps it instead of expecting it in order;
# run-smoke.sh also checks the saved config carries the key without whitespace and mode 0600
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect OpenRouter API key
sleep 0.3
send sk-or-v1-fakefakefakefakefakefakefakefakefake\r
expect Verify now\?
sleep 0.3
send n
expect sess \$
expect Say hi
sleep 0.3
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
